` "eu-oaz72.175: a wrapper function whose frame holds the list head while a
   closed `+` lambda is threaded through a strict fold must not pin the list.
   The `.( )` tail position is deliberate: a `.result` binding would be a thunk
   holding an update frame per level, which is a different (stack) retention."
fs(op, i, l): l nil? then(i, { a: op(i, l head) }.(seq(a, fs(op, a, l tail))))

c3(l): fs(+, 0, l)

x: range(0, 200000) c3
